<section class="review-section" id="faq">
<h2><svg class="neon-icon" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><line x1="12" x2="12.01" y1="17" y2="17"></line></svg> Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Do I need to know Grasshopper to use Finch 3D?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, Finch 3D is a Grasshopper plugin, so you need working knowledge of both Rhino and Grasshopper. However, Finch provides excellent tutorials to help you get started with their specific components.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">How accurate are the environmental simulations?</div><div class="faq-answer">Finch's daylight and ventilation simulations are suitable for early-stage design decisions and comparative analysis. For final building certification, you'll still need dedicated simulation tools like Radiance or EnergyPlus.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can I use Finch for detailed design development?</div><div class="faq-answer">Finch excels at early-stage massing and optimization. For detailed design, you'll need to export to traditional BIM tools. Think of Finch as a design exploration and decision-making tool.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">What's the difference between Finch and native Grasshopper optimization?</div><div class="faq-answer">Finch uses advanced AI algorithms specifically trained for architectural problems. It's faster and more user-friendly than setting up custom optimization with Galapagos or other native Grasshopper tools.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Does the free tier have enough features for students?</div><div class="faq-answer">Yes, the free tier is specifically designed for educational use. It has monthly optimization limits but includes all the core analysis features students need for coursework and thesis projects.</div></div>
<div class="faq-item"><div class="faq-question">Can multiple team members work on the same optimization?</div><div class="faq-answer">Team plans include collaboration features that allow sharing optimization setups and results. However, real-time collaborative editing isn't currently supported—it's more about sharing libraries and best practices.</div></div>
